            "enHtml": "<h4>Direct Digital System — Advantages &amp; Disadvantages</h4>\n                  <p><strong>Advantages:</strong></p>\n                  <ul>\n                    <li><mark class=\"hl-func\" data-pair=\"1\">a- Low radiation dose</mark></li>\n                    <li><mark class=\"hl-func\" data-pair=\"2\">b- Darkroom is not required as instant image is viewed with eliminated hazards of film processing procedure.</mark></li>\n                    <li><mark class=\"hl-func\" data-pair=\"3\">c- The quality of the image is consistent</mark></li>\n                    <li><mark class=\"hl-exam\" data-pair=\"4\">d- Diagnostic capability is increased through digital enhancement and enlargement of specific areas for closer examination</mark></li>\n                    <li><mark class=\"hl-func\" data-pair=\"5\">e- Storages and archiving of patient information</mark></li>\n                  </ul>\n                  <p><strong>Disadvantages:</strong></p>\n                  <ul>\n                    <li><mark class=\"hl-warn\" data-pair=\"6\">a- Expensive.</mark></li>\n                    <li><mark class=\"hl-warn\" data-pair=\"7\">b- Life expectancy of CCD is not fixed.</mark></li>\n                    <li><mark class=\"hl-warn\" data-pair=\"8\">c- Bulky sensor with cable attachment, which can make placement in mouth difficult.</mark></li>\n                    <li><mark class=\"hl-warn\" data-pair=\"9\">d- Large disk space required to store images</mark></li>\n                  </ul>",
